00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.010
And honestly, you know,
it's always such a,

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:06.350
I think it's a little bit
different because now it may be

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:08.360
we're performing in similar space,

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:09.530
it's, every time it's different.

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:13.180
So I'm just open to the newness
and I know we're all excited

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:16.550
to just hear great music and
have a good, have a good night.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:19.086
- Yeah and I mean, while
we're all navigating the new,

00:01:19.086 --> 00:01:21.240
it, at least we're being able to navigate,

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.474
at least we're at least out of our houses,

00:01:23.474 --> 00:01:25.290
we're able to be somewhere
and actually perform.

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:27.510
As artists, like, you feel
like it's your duty right now.

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:30.670
Like your job to kind of,
you know, not distract,

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:33.740
but just kind of bring a
little hope, you know, more so,

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:35.600
but I want to talk about
this 'cause you created

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:38.340
a $1 billion fund to support
black owned businesses,

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:39.230
which is amazing.

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:42.440
The NFL has contributed,
how can others help?

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:43.390
- Absolutely.

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:44.250
This is a, you know,

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:47.190
this is a really, something I'm
very, very passionate about.

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:49.080
There's so many people that
are thinking like this,

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.510
thinking about this.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.870
Obviously we know that it's the time,

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:54.600
we see the inequities that are happening

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:55.433
right in front of us.

00:01:55.433 --> 00:01:59.800
We know that it's time to
really empower black America.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:04.400
And so this is something that
is big, big, big, big for me.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:05.620
I'm so, so proud.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:07.800
And I feel like so many corporations,

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:11.320
institutions and organizations
really do want to be invited

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:14.360
to the table to figure
out how to contribute.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:16.530
And so this is a conversation
we're gonna be having,

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:18.320
we're creating it now, building it all up.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:21.230
The response has been unbelievable.

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:23.340
It's gonna be focused on black businesses

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:27.040
and black investments
invested by black investors.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.520
black schools, black banks,
you know, black communities.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:33.600
It's really powerful
and I love the response.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:36.120
So thank you for bringing
it up and yes, I'll be,

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:38.520
I'll be telling you more about it a lot.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:39.820
So this is the beginning.

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:41.450
- It's important.

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:42.871
And now it's the time like, you know,

00:02:42.871 --> 00:02:44.460
I've been hearing everyone
talk about how crappy 2020 is

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:48.310
and yes it is but at
the same time, you know,

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:50.330
I think everything's
have to go just around.,

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:52.260
Just kind of be messy before
you can actually fix the

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.280
problem and notice how bad the problem is.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:56.570
So I love that you're doing this.

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:57.590
I think it's very important.

00:02:57.590 --> 00:02:59.580
All right, so Alicia's new album

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:01.820
is called "Alicia" and it's out right now.

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:03.620
So if you're smart, you'll go get it.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:04.720
I just have a quick question.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:06.750
I mean, is this new album a
very personal one for you?

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:09.200
You've you've named it after
your name, obviously, so.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:12.219
- This is definitely the one
that I know myself the best.

00:03:12.219 --> 00:03:15.210
I've totally not, I would
have never been able to call

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:17.580
my previous albums, "Alicia,"
just because, you know,

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:19.340
of course I've always been myself,

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:21.560
but I didn't know myself as well.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:23.830
And this particular album is
really about the different

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:27.450
nuances and sides of us because
there's so many different

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:29.760
pieces that make us a whole person.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:31.010
But so many times we don't get to

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.550
express those sides, right?

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:34.350
Like at the job, we're one way,

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:36.200
with our family, we're one way,

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.690
with our kids, we're one way.

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:40.060
When do we get to kind of
explore the parts of ourselves

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:40.893
we don't know?

00:03:40.893 --> 00:03:43.990
So that's been something that
I've been learning about and,

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.670
and, and really it's, it's
poured into this music.

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:47.910
It's poured into the writing.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:50.690
It's poured into the
diversity that you hear

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:53.250
and the response has been so crazy.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:56.040
I've been so proud and
excited for the love

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.200
everybody has for it.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.113
- That's really great, man,
I'm super proud of you.

00:04:00.113 --> 00:04:01.205
That's so cool.

00:04:01.205 --> 00:04:02.863
And everybody needs music
now more than ever, you know,

00:04:02.863 --> 00:04:03.970
like it's, it's nice.

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:05.980
Feel a little hope, a little
distraction, all of it.

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:07.140
Well, let's, let's talk.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.805
I wanna, I want some stories
about some of the tracks.

00:04:09.805 --> 00:04:12.110
I was listening last
night and this morning.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:14.890
And so, so maybe the most powerful song

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:17.460
and it's incredibly hard to listen to

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:20.940
if you're a mama as well
is "Perfect Way to Die."

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:23.190
It's the story of a
mother's grief after her son

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:24.563
is shot by police.

00:04:24.563 --> 00:04:27.970
How difficult, I mean you're a mama and,

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:30.530
and part of the community
that's being attacked right now.

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:32.280
You know, so how hard is it that?

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:33.380
- I mean, it's devastating.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:36.070
Obviously we all can see
it, no matter where we live,

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:38.730
no matter how we grew up, you know,

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:41.670
we can all see what's happening
so clearly and evidently,

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:43.400
and I, and I know that we're all outraged.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:46.660
We're all, you know, just,
we don't accept it anymore.

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:49.000
You know, this is not the
way that it's supposed to be

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:50.690
and we will not accept it anymore.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.380
But to write that song,

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:56.240
just a sliver of that
conversation, that emotion,

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:00.530
that feeling of, of losing your child

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:02.840
because somebody murdered them because

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:05.030
they judged them in some way
or thought they were gonna

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:06.990
cause harm that they weren't going to.

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:09.520
I mean, the grief, I can't even imagine.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:11.180
There is no perfect way to die and

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:13.870
definitely not at the
hands of police brutality

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:17.540
but bringing that to the
forefront and being able to have

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:18.920
that be a conversation at work.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.910
We're all talking about, thinking about,

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:22.880
obviously going into this election,

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:25.570
thinking about how do we want
to show up for ourselves,

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:26.550
for our communities,

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:29.030
what do we want to
demand from our country?

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:31.850
You know, it's a really
powerful conversation

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:34.080
to be having and, and just
the encouragement for us

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:36.670
to show up, to start to make
the shifts or the changes

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:38.830
that we we know are needed.

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:41.010
- Yeah, and I think we, we take advantage

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:42.320
that we're so lucky.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:44.790
We're so fortunate to
have that vote, you know,

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:47.140
and I think we're, in this
country, we get so comfortable.

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:48.760
We get in our little
comfort zones sometimes,

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:52.130
and you don't realize how
important it is to vote.

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:55.030
Like, and anyway but Breonna
Taylor was in the video

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:56.360
for that song as well.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:59.540
Alicia has been pushing for
justice for her and this summer,

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:02.970
she made another video with
Breonna's mom, Tamika Palmer,

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:06.310
activist, Tamika Mallory,
and the rapper Rhapsody.

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:10.520
So Alicia, do you feel hopeful
in the fight right now?

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:12.290
- You know, I mean, I'll be honest.

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:15.260
I, I, I'm disappointed.

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:17.510
I'm very disappointed, I'm frustrated.

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:19.320
And I think we all are.

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:21.920
It's just, it's just enough with the,

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:24.290
the actions that are
never held accountable.

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:26.580
It's just enough, you know, and I,

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:29.790
I feel like it definitely feels,

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:33.720
I know it's wrong and I
know that it has to change.

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:37.380
And I do feel inspired to
continue to show up and continue

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:40.020
to be an active part
of humanity, you know,

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:43.410
because we all have to
care about what's going on.

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:45.900
And that's one thing that
I do see, I truly do.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:48.325
I see the whole world,

00:06:48.325 --> 00:06:51.640
France, Paris, London, you know,

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:55.265
the whole of America
really for the first time

00:06:55.265 --> 00:06:58.770
showing up and saying and
speaking loud, you know?

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:01.850
And, and, and so in that way,
I do feel inspired that we,

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:04.930
the people who do make the changes,

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:07.160
because I know sometimes
it's hard to believe.

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.230
You know, we think, you
know, this, this, this,

00:07:09.230 --> 00:07:11.580
this unseen government
kind of does everything

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:12.790
and we have no control over it.

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:14.767
Sometimes we can feel like that

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:17.660
but we do have the power,
we do wield the power.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:20.300
And so I do feel inspired
to continue going,

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:23.550
but I do feel disappointed
that more justice wasn't due

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:25.320
for Breonna and for all the people

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:26.900
who have lost their lives,

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:29.340
you know, been murdered
by police brutality.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:30.680
- Agreed.

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:32.420
Well, you've, I want
to talk about this too.

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:33.736
You have so many things.

00:07:33.736 --> 00:07:35.750
You, you're, you're just like
that lady doing everything.

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:36.583
I love it.

00:07:36.583 --> 00:07:39.090
So you you've also
branched out from music.

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:40.723
So tell me about Keys Soulcare.

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:43.280
- You know, it's, it's, it's, it's a,

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:44.720
it's a lifestyle brand,

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:46.500
it's a concept, it's a thought.

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:50.170
It's going, it was started
with my personal journey

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:53.670
to find the right skin care for myself.

00:07:53.670 --> 00:07:57.060
And it's been a tricky situation for me

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:58.440
since I was quite young.

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:01.030
And it's always been a dream
of me to create something

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:03.560
that would be just good for my skin,

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:06.700
but not only for the
outside, for the inside.

00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:08.450
And I realized that we focus so much,

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:11.480
we have skin care and nail care
and body care and hair care.

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:14.680
We have all this care, but
we don't have soul care.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:16.068
You know?

00:08:16.068 --> 00:08:19.340
So I created a Keys Soulcare
in the essence of that

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:20.960
and it's gonna be many things,

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:23.480
but right now it's really
just about community

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:24.930
and it's about ritual

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:29.750
and it's about talking about
how can we focus on ourselves,

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:31.400
fill ourselves up and our souls.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:35.220
And so that's why Keys Soulcare
was born and I'm excited.

00:08:35.220 --> 00:08:36.720
- Well, here's the thing too.

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:38.730
I love when something is organic,

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:42.640
but Alicia is launching Key's
Soulcare in December, y'all,

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:44.180
which also happens to be the month

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:47.270
of my favorite holiday. Christmas.

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:48.860
As you know, I'm a firm believer

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:51.730
that the holidays can be
celebrated on any given day

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:53.019
of the year.

00:08:53.019 --> 00:08:54.678
Oh my gosh, what's that noise?

00:08:54.678 --> 00:08:56.685
Oh my gosh, it's our very first

00:08:56.685 --> 00:08:58.578
Ambush Christmas this season.

00:08:58.578 --> 00:09:01.161
Man, it's Christmas in October.

00:09:03.279 --> 00:09:05.339
You're welcome.

00:09:05.339 --> 00:09:07.089
I am being dumped on.

00:09:10.204 --> 00:09:12.130
Everywhere, that was awesome.

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:13.790
It's like I'm in a video.

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:14.670
Well I kinda am.

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:17.080
Okay, so that means
it's gift time, people.

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:19.470
And Soulcare starts here.

00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:21.478
Alicia Keys and Key Soulcare

00:09:21.478 --> 00:09:23.540
want to help you give
yourself a moment of calm.

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:25.230
It's still snowing.

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:27.560
They want to give you a moment of calm

